\begin{abstract}
We present ACSE-v4.0, a sovereign multi-scale simulation and hardware
architecture that couples real astrophysical datasets (Gaia DR3, LIGO/Virgo,
JWST) to a crystal-substrate computational matrix and a resonance-coupled
entropy engine. The system integrates a Langasite-based phonon-polariton
substrate, high-density tensor simulation grids, and a cryptographic pipeline
driven by chaotic maps seeded from astrophysical telemetry. We report
Tier-Omega stress-test results, Hamiltonian residual convergence, substrate
stability under thermal shock, and cryptographic entropy density approaching
ideal randomness.
\end{abstract}

